      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and 1000 mg is five times the labeled maximum of 200 mg per day. That limit applies whatever has been claimed about approval.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can enter up to 200 mg once daily right now. Titrating toward that is the usual approach after standard dosing fails.\n- **Use pharmacy and prescriber channels for an above-label dose.** If the specialist wants more than 200 mg, the specialist or the attending would need to place the order directly. It would typically go through pharmacy review and any required off-label or high-dose approval. I can't enter it for them.\n- **Add a note to a compliant order.** I can include a note such as \"Specialist recommends higher dose; pending pharmacy/attending review.\"\n\nWould you like me to enter sertraline at 200 mg once daily or a lower dose? Or would you rather take the 1000 mg request through the formal review route?"
      }
